## Reflection

This project introduced sequential logic, where outputs depend on both the current inputs and the previous state.

I learned how a D Flip-Flop stores one bit of information and only updates its output on the rising edge of the clock. This was a significant shift from combinational logic, where outputs change immediately when inputs change.

The biggest challenge was understanding why the output does not change immediately when the input changes. By studying the waveform, I realized that the output is only updated on the rising edge of the clock, which is the key characteristic of sequential logic.

